    <l n="13" para="true">IX. <i>Externorum sensuum primus ta-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>ctus est, qui quidem per omnes corporis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>partes diffusus est, attamen in homine</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>proprium organum habet cutem, eam ma-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>xime, quae est in vola manus, &amp; in ex-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>tremis acinis digitorum.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">§. 1. Inter sensus externos alius est</l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>ordo dignitatis</i>, alius <i>necessitatis</i>. Secun-</l>
    <l n="21">dum illum visui primitas adscribi solet,</l>
    <l n="22">ob obiecti dignitatem, modi propaga-</l>
    <l n="23">tionis longitudinem, &amp; organi structu-</l>
    <l n="24">ram: verum secundum hunc primum</l>
    <l n="25">locum tenet tactus. Nam 1. omnibus</l>
    <l n="26">animalibus competit. 2. per plures par-</l>
    <l n="27">tes diffusus est, &amp; 3. in organis quo-</l>
